IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cpp-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cp1-nouns`
IMPORT `cp1-months-helpers`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part I, Division B -- section 12: CONTRIBUTORY SALARY AND WAGES.
--
-- The contributory salary and wages of a person for a year are the person's income for the year from pensionable
-- employment (computed under the Income Tax Act) plus certain deductions, less the income received (a) before
-- eighteen, (b) in a month excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability, (c) after sixty-five when a
-- retirement pension is payable and the person has elected to exclude the income, and (d) after seventy.
--
-- Whether income is excluded depends on the date it was received, so the income is a list of receipts
-- (`cp1 Income receipt`). Every boundary in subsection 12(1) falls on the first day of a month (section 2(2) puts
-- the age at the first day of the month after the birthday; the election takes effect on the first day of a
-- month), so the tests below are made on the month of the receipt.
--
-- Ages go through the keel's section 2(2) rule with `any other provision`: paragraphs 12(1)(a), (c) and (d) are not
-- among the ten places where the actual birthday governs.
--
-- out of range: the Income Tax Act is not part of this text: the income "computed in accordance with" it, and the deductions made in computing it, are plain inputs.
-- out of range: section 49 (piece cp3): the contributory period and its excluded months.
-- out of range: section 44 (piece cp3) and section 67 (piece cp5): "a retirement pension is payable".
-- out of range: regulation 83.1 (piece cr1): the election of subsection 12(1.1) is made or revoked by providing the prescribed form to an employer of the person.
-- out of range: regulations 29.1 and 30 (piece cr1), made under subsection 7(1): the extent to which an Indian's income from otherwise excepted employment is included.
-- out of range: the Public Service Superannuation Act is not part of this text: "salary" as that Act defines it.

§ `Division B -- Calculation of Contributions`

§§ `Section 12(1.1) -- the election to exclude income after sixty-five`

-- src:342 | Election
-- src:343 | (1.1) An election referred to in subparagraph (1)(c)(ii)
-- src:344 | (a) shall be made or revoked in the prescribed form and manner;
-- src:345 | (b) shall commence to have effect on the first day of the month following the month in which it is made;
-- src:346 | (c) shall cease to have effect on the first day of the month following the month in which it is revoked;
-- src:347 | (d) may be made only once in a year;
-- src:348 | (e) may not be revoked in the year in which it is made;
-- src:349 | (f) may not be made in a year in which an election is revoked; and
-- src:350 | (g) is deemed to be an election in respect of the person’s income from all pensionable employment and in respect of their self-employed earnings.
@ref Act s 12(1.1)(b) (src:345)
GIVEN `date the election is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 12(1.1)(b) — the first day on which the election has effect` `date the election is made` MEANS
    `the month following the month of a date` `date the election is made`

@ref Act s 12(1.1)(c) (src:346)
GIVEN `date the election is revoked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 12(1.1)(c) — the first day on which the election ceases to have effect` `date the election is revoked` MEANS
    `the month following the month of a date` `date the election is revoked`

-- Whether an election has effect in a month: it has effect from the first day it commences until the day before the first
-- day it ceases (paragraphs (b) and (c)). Not a provision of its own.
@ref Act s 12(1.1) (src:345-346)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `date the election is made` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date the election is revoked` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12(1.1) — an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) has effect in a month` month `date the election is made` `date the election is revoked` MEANS
    CONSIDER `date the election is made`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST made THEN
            `the month of a date` month AT LEAST `s 12(1.1)(b) — the first day on which the election has effect` made
        AND (CONSIDER `date the election is revoked`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
             WHEN JUST revoked THEN `the month of a date` month LESS THAN `s 12(1.1)(c) — the first day on which the election ceases to have effect` revoked)

@ref Act s 12(1.1)(a) (src:344)
GIVEN `the election is made or revoked in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12(1.1)(a) — the election or the revocation is valid in form` `the election is made or revoked in the prescribed form and manner` MEANS
    `the election is made or revoked in the prescribed form and manner`

@ref Act s 12(1.1)(d) (src:347)
GIVEN `an election has already been made in the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12(1.1)(d) — the election may be made in the year` `an election has already been made in the year` MEANS
    NOT `an election has already been made in the year`

@ref Act s 12(1.1)(e) (src:348)
GIVEN `year in which the election was made` IS A NUMBER
      `year in which the election is revoked` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12(1.1)(e) — the election may be revoked in the year` `year in which the election was made` `year in which the election is revoked` MEANS
    NOT (`year in which the election is revoked` EQUALS `year in which the election was made`)

@ref Act s 12(1.1)(f) (src:349)
GIVEN `an election is revoked in the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12(1.1)(f) — the election may be made in the year` `an election is revoked in the year` MEANS
    NOT `an election is revoked in the year`

-- An election may be made only if it is in the prescribed form and manner (a), no election has been made in the
-- year (d), and none is revoked in it (f).
@ref Act s 12(1.1) (src:343-349)
GIVEN `the election is made or revoked in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an election has already been made in the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an election is revoked in the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12(1.1) — a valid election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) may be made` `the election is made or revoked in the prescribed form and manner` `an election has already been made in the year` `an election is revoked in the year` MEANS
        `s 12(1.1)(a) — the election or the revocation is valid in form` `the election is made or revoked in the prescribed form and manner`
    AND `s 12(1.1)(d) — the election may be made in the year` `an election has already been made in the year`
    AND `s 12(1.1)(f) — the election may be made in the year` `an election is revoked in the year`

-- A revocation is valid if it is in the prescribed form and manner (a) and not in the year the election was made (e).
@ref Act s 12(1.1) (src:343-348)
GIVEN `the election is made or revoked in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `year in which the election was made` IS A NUMBER
      `year in which the election is revoked` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12(1.1) — a valid revocation of the election may be made` `the election is made or revoked in the prescribed form and manner` `year in which the election was made` `year in which the election is revoked` MEANS
        `s 12(1.1)(a) — the election or the revocation is valid in form` `the election is made or revoked in the prescribed form and manner`
    AND `s 12(1.1)(e) — the election may be revoked in the year` `year in which the election was made` `year in which the election is revoked`

-- Paragraph (g): the election is deemed an election in respect of the income from all pensionable employment and of
-- the self-employed earnings.
DECLARE `cp1 Kind of income an election may exclude` IS ONE OF
    `income from a pensionable employment`
    `self-employed earnings`
    `another kind of income`

@ref Act s 12(1.1)(g) (src:350)
GIVEN kind IS A `cp1 Kind of income an election may exclude`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12(1.1)(g) — an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) is deemed an election in respect of the kind of income` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `income from a pensionable employment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `self-employed earnings` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another kind of income` THEN FALSE

§§ `Section 12(1) -- the income that is left out`

-- src:334 | Amount of contributory salary and wages
-- src:335 | 12 (1) The amount of the contributory salary and wages of a person for a year is the person’s income for the year from pensionable employment, computed in accordance with the Income Tax Act, plus any deductions for the year made in computing that income otherwise than under paragraph 8(1)(c) of that Act, but does not include any such income received by the person
-- src:336 | (a) before he reaches eighteen years of age;
-- src:337 | (b) during any month that is excluded from that person’s contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability;
-- src:338 | (c) after they reach sixty-five years of age if
-- src:339 | (i) a retirement pension is payable to them under this Act or under a provincial pension plan, and
-- src:340 | (ii) subject to subsection (1.1), they make an election to exclude the income; or
-- src:341 | (d) after they reach seventy years of age.
-- The four exclusions test the date on which the income is received. Each takes the facts about the person and the date.

@ref Act s 12(1)(a) (src:336)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
      `date the income is received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12(1)(a) — the income is received before the person reaches eighteen years of age` facts `date the income is received` MEANS
    NOT `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision`
            `any other provision`
            (facts's `date of birth of the person`)
            18
            `date the income is received`

@ref Act s 12(1)(b) (src:337)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
      `date the income is received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12(1)(b) — the income is received during a month excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability` facts `date the income is received` MEANS
    `a month falls in one of the month periods`
        `date the income is received`
        (facts's `months excluded from the contributory period of the person by reason of disability`)

@ref Act s 12(1)(c) (src:338-340)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
      `date the income is received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12(1)(c) — the income is received after the person reaches sixty-five years of age while a retirement pension is payable and an election to exclude it has effect` facts `date the income is received` MEANS
        `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision`
            `any other provision`
            (facts's `date of birth of the person`)
            65
            `date the income is received`
    -- (i) a retirement pension is payable to them
    AND `a month is at or after the month of an optional date` `date the income is received` (facts's `month from which a retirement pension is payable to the person`)
    -- (ii) subject to subsection (1.1), they make an election to exclude the income
    AND `s 12(1.1) — an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) has effect in a month`
            `date the income is received`
            (facts's `date the person makes an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii)`)
            (facts's `date the person revokes the election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii)`)

@ref Act s 12(1)(d) (src:341)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
      `date the income is received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12(1)(d) — the income is received after the person reaches seventy years of age` facts `date the income is received` MEANS
    `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision`
        `any other provision`
        (facts's `date of birth of the person`)
        70
        `date the income is received`

@ref Act s 12(1) (src:334-341)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
      `date the income is received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12(1) — income received on a date is not included in the contributory salary and wages` facts `date the income is received` MEANS
        `s 12(1)(a) — the income is received before the person reaches eighteen years of age` facts `date the income is received`
    OR  `s 12(1)(b) — the income is received during a month excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability` facts `date the income is received`
    OR  `s 12(1)(c) — the income is received after the person reaches sixty-five years of age while a retirement pension is payable and an election to exclude it has effect` facts `date the income is received`
    OR  `s 12(1)(d) — the income is received after the person reaches seventy years of age` facts `date the income is received`

-- The amount: the income received, less the receipts that are left out, plus the deductions.
-- The deductions are added in full: the text dates only the income received (NOTES.md, fork register).
@ref Act s 12(1) (src:334-335)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
      receipts IS A LIST OF `cp1 Income receipt`
      `deductions for the year made in computing that income otherwise than under paragraph 8(1)(c) of the Income Tax Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 12(1) — the contributory salary and wages of a person for a year` facts receipts `deductions for the year made in computing that income otherwise than under paragraph 8(1)(c) of the Income Tax Act` MEANS
    (sum (map (GIVEN receipt YIELD receipt's `amount of the income received`)
              (filter (GIVEN receipt YIELD NOT `s 12(1) — income received on a date is not included in the contributory salary and wages` facts (receipt's `date the income is received`)) receipts)))
    PLUS `deductions for the year made in computing that income otherwise than under paragraph 8(1)(c) of the Income Tax Act`

§§ `Section 12(1.2) to (3) -- continuing employers, public servants, Indians and provincial plans`

-- src:351 | Calculation of contributory salary and wages
-- src:352 | (1.2) If a person does not revoke — in respect of an employer — an election in the prescribed form and manner, the contributory salary and wages referred to in paragraphs 8(1)(a) and (1.1)(a), subsection 8(1.2), paragraphs 9(1)(a) and (1.1)(a) and subsection 9(1.2) do not, for the purposes of those provisions, include income from that employment. However, the person may — in respect of that income — make an election under subsection 13(3) and pay the contributions required under section 10 within one year after the person’s balance-due day.
@ref Act s 12(1.2) (src:351-352)
GIVEN `the person does not revoke, in respect of the employer, an election in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributory salary and wages paid by the employer, as subsection (1) works them out` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 12(1.2) — the contributory salary and wages from an employer for sections 8 and 9` `the person does not revoke, in respect of the employer, an election in the prescribed form and manner` `the contributory salary and wages paid by the employer, as subsection (1) works them out` MEANS
    IF `the person does not revoke, in respect of the employer, an election in the prescribed form and manner`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the contributory salary and wages paid by the employer, as subsection (1) works them out`

-- "However, the person may -- in respect of that income -- make an election under subsection 13(3) and pay the
-- contributions required under section 10 within one year after the person's balance-due day."
@ref Act s 12(1.2) (src:352)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `date of death of the person` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date the person makes the election under subsection 13(3) and pays the contributions required under section 10` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12(1.2) — the person may make an election under subsection 13(3) and pay the contributions required under section 10 on a date` year `date of death of the person` `date the person makes the election under subsection 13(3) and pays the contributions required under section 10` MEANS
    `a date is within a time limit after a start date`
        `date the person makes the election under subsection 13(3) and pays the contributions required under section 10`
        (`s 2(1) — the balance-due day of a person for a year` year `date of death of the person`)
        (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 1)

-- src:353 | Idem
-- src:354 | (2) In the case of a person who is a contributor under the Public Service Superannuation Act, there shall be included in computing the amount of that person’s contributory salary and wages for a year the amount of his salary, as defined in that Act, that is not otherwise included in computing income for the purposes of the Income Tax Act.
@ref Act s 12(2) (src:353-354)
GIVEN `the person is a contributor under the Public Service Superannuation Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's salary, as defined in that Act, not otherwise included in computing income for the purposes of the Income Tax Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 12(2) — the salary of a contributor under the Public Service Superannuation Act included in the contributory salary and wages` `the person is a contributor under the Public Service Superannuation Act` `the person's salary, as defined in that Act, not otherwise included in computing income for the purposes of the Income Tax Act` MEANS
    IF `the person is a contributor under the Public Service Superannuation Act`
    THEN JUST `the person's salary, as defined in that Act, not otherwise included in computing income for the purposes of the Income Tax Act`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:355 | Idem
-- src:356 | (2.1) In the case of an Indian, as defined in the Indian Act, to the extent provided by regulations pursuant to subsection 7(1) and subject to any conditions prescribed by those regulations, there shall be included in computing the amount of that person’s contributory salary and wages for a year the amount of his income from employment that would otherwise be excepted pursuant to paragraph 6(2)(j.1).
@ref Act s 12(2.1) (src:355-356)
GIVEN `the person is an Indian as defined in the Indian Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the income from employment otherwise excepted under paragraph 6(2)(j.1) that the regulations made under subsection 7(1) provide to be included` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 12(2.1) — the income of an Indian from employment otherwise excepted that is included in the contributory salary and wages` `the person is an Indian as defined in the Indian Act` `the amount of the income from employment otherwise excepted under paragraph 6(2)(j.1) that the regulations made under subsection 7(1) provide to be included` MEANS
    IF `the person is an Indian as defined in the Indian Act`
    THEN JUST `the amount of the income from employment otherwise excepted under paragraph 6(2)(j.1) that the regulations made under subsection 7(1) provide to be included`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:357 | Remuneration paid in respect of employment in province
-- src:358 | (3) A reference in this Act to the contributory salary and wages of a person for a year shall, in relation to any remuneration paid to him in respect of pensionable employment in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan, be construed as a reference to his income for the year from that employment as that income is required to be computed under the provincial pension plan of that province.
@ref Act s 12(3) (src:357-358)
GIVEN `the remuneration is paid in respect of pensionable employment in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the income for the year from that employment as the provincial pension plan requires it to be computed` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributory salary and wages as this Act works them out` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 12(3) — the contributory salary and wages for remuneration paid in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` `the remuneration is paid in respect of pensionable employment in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` `the income for the year from that employment as the provincial pension plan requires it to be computed` `the contributory salary and wages as this Act works them out` MEANS
    IF `the remuneration is paid in respect of pensionable employment in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan`
    THEN `the income for the year from that employment as the provincial pension plan requires it to be computed`
    ELSE `the contributory salary and wages as this Act works them out`

-- Subsection 12(1) with the inclusions of subsections 12(2) and 12(2.1) added: "there shall be included in computing
-- the amount of that person's contributory salary and wages for a year". Subsection 12(3) then applies to remuneration
-- paid in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan.
@ref Act s 12 (src:334-358)
GIVEN `the amount under subsection (1)` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount under subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the amount under subsection (2.1)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 12 — the contributory salary and wages of a person for a year, with the inclusions of subsections (2) and (2.1)` `the amount under subsection (1)` `the amount under subsection (2)` `the amount under subsection (2.1)` MEANS
        `the amount under subsection (1)`
    PLUS fromMaybe 0 `the amount under subsection (2)`
    PLUS fromMaybe 0 `the amount under subsection (2.1)`
